\subsection{C.1 PDE Solvers}

Partial Differential Equation (PDE) solvers are used in Axon-FP,
Chronos-V, and Stratos-Core. All PDE solvers satisfy the following
requirements:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Total Variation Diminishing (TVD),
    \item deterministic time-stepping,
    \item bounded spatial discretization,
    \item strict IEEE 754 floating-point compliance,
    \item reproducible multi-threading (Rayon),
    \item reproducible GPU execution (OpenCL/CUDA).
\end{itemize}

\subsubsection{C.1.1 Navier–Stokes Solver}

Used in Stratos-Core for atmospheric flux fields.

\[
\frac{\partial \mathbf{u}}{\partial t}
+ (\mathbf{u} \cdot \nabla)\mathbf{u}
= -\frac{1}{\rho}\nabla p + \nu \nabla^2 \mathbf{u}.
\]

Specifications:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Spatial discretization: 4th-order finite volume,
    \item Time-stepping: deterministic Runge–Kutta (RK4),
    \item Stability: CFL-controlled,
    \item Boundary conditions: radiative, convective, reflective.
\end{itemize}

